# The database is a build artifact, not a source file -- always
# regenerable from migrate_s9.py (the workbook, rounds 1-11) +
# results/*.csv (deckfield add-results, round 12 onward, replayed in
# order). Never commit it.
#
# That invariant only holds if every ingested matchday's CSV is actually
# kept here. If a round ever exists ONLY in the database, recover it with
#   python3 deckfield_cli.py export-results
# which writes every post-workbook round back out in the exact add-results
# format -- byte-identical to what deckfield.html's Download CSV produces,
# so re-running it over an up-to-date results/ is a no-op.
deckfield.db
deckfield_test*.db
deckfield_*_backup*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor files
*.swp
*~
